
GRAPH DATA STRUCTURE - INTRODUCTION 
=======================================================

A graph G = (V, E) has vertices V = {v1, v2, v3, v4, v5} and edges E.

 - Undirected graph : edge has no direction   (v1 --- v2)
 - Directed graph   : edge has a direction    (v1 ---> v2)


1. WALK
-------
A sequence of vertices where consecutive vertices are joined by an edge.
Vertices and edges CAN repeat.

   v1 --- v2 --- v3 --- v4 --- v5

 Walk : v1 -> v2 -> v3 -> v2 -> v3 -> v4 -> v5
        (v2 and v3 repeat - allowed)


2. PATH
-------
A walk with NO repeated vertices.

   v1 --- v2 --- v3 --- v4 --- v5

 Path     : v1 -> v2 -> v3 -> v4 -> v5      (valid)
 Not path : v1 -> v2 -> v3 -> v2            (v2 repeats, only a walk)

 Every path is a walk, but not every walk is a path.


3. CYCLIC GRAPH
---------------
A graph that contains a cycle: a path that starts and ends at the
same vertex.

 a) Undirected cyclic

        v1 --- v2
        |       |
        |       |
        v4 --- v3 --- v5

    Cycle : v1 - v2 - v3 - v4 - v1

 b) Directed cyclic

        v1 ---> v2 ---> v3
                ^        |
                |        v
                +------- v4 ---> v5

    Cycle : v2 -> v3 -> v4 -> v2


4. ACYCLIC GRAPH
----------------
A graph with NO cycle.

 a) Undirected Acyclic Graph (Tree)
    Connected, no cycle. Edges = vertices - 1 = 4.

              v1
             /  \
           v2    v3
          /  \
        v4    v5

    Edges : v1-v2, v1-v3, v2-v4, v2-v5

 b) Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)
    Directed edges, no directed cycle. You can never come back to a
    vertex by following the arrows.

            +--> v2 --+
            |         v
           v1         v4 ---> v5
            |         ^
            +--> v3 --+

    Edges : v1->v2, v1->v3, v2->v4, v3->v4, v4->v5
    Topological order : v1, v2, v3, v4, v5

    Uses : task scheduling, course prerequisites, build systems.


QUICK COMPARISON
----------------

Term  | Repeat vertices? | Repeat edges? | Closed (start = end)?
------|------------------|---------------|----------------------
Walk  | Yes              | Yes           | Optional
Path  | No               | No            | No
Cycle | Only start = end | No            | Yes

Graph type                       | Direction | Has cycle?
---------------------------------|-----------|-----------
Undirected cyclic                | No        | Yes
Undirected acyclic (tree/forest) | No        | No
Directed cyclic                  | Yes       | Yes
DAG                              | Yes       | No
